# UnityEngine 2D physics and sprites → Godot 2D nodes.
#
# A 2D Unity GameObject maps to a Node2D-derived node (RigidBody2D / Area2D / StaticBody2D with
# CollisionShape2D children, Sprite2D). Unity 2D uses Y-up; Godot 2D uses Y-down, so vectors
# are converted with `U.v2_to_gd` / `U.v2_from_gd` (y negated) where positions/forces cross over.

